{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For</b> — the meaning is long life, like 'men of great measure,' and figuratively he said, 'for weeping spends the night.' Or the verb may be elided, as in: 'who bore her.'" "And the meaning of 'at evening he lodges' — 'he who lodges with weeping, and in the morning with joy,' for the construct noun is missing throughout the verse, as in: 'Is it found in the house of YHWH.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The phrase 'men of great measure' (אנשי מדות גדולות) is opaque; possibly referring to long-lived patriarchs or to a known midrashic/rabbinic expression. The ellipsis example 'אשר ילדה אותה' is not a direct biblical quotation and its referent is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:59.483619486Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}